.TH "RESTORE-OBJECT"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
restore-object \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This operation is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Restores an archived copy of an object back into Amazon S3
.sp
This functionality is not supported for Amazon S3 on Outposts.
.sp
This action performs the following types of requests:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrestore an archive\fP \- Restore an archived object
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information about the \fBS3\fP structure in the request body, see the following:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%PutObject\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%Managing Access with ACLs\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%Protecting Data Using Server\-Side Encryption\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP
.sp
Permissions
.UNINDENT
.sp
To use this operation, you must have permissions to perform the \fBs3:RestoreObject\fP action. The bucket owner has this permission by default and can grant this permission to others. For more information about permissions, see \fI\%Permissions Related to Bucket Subresource Operations\fP and \fI\%Managing Access Permissions to Your Amazon S3 Resources\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Restoring objects
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Objects that you archive to the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval or S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class, and S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Archive or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Deep Archive tiers, are not accessible in real time. For objects in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval or S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage classes, you must first initiate a restore request, and then wait until a temporary copy of the object is available. If you want a permanent copy of the object, create a copy of it in the Amazon S3 Standard storage class in your S3 bucket. To access an archived object, you must restore the object for the duration (number of days) that you specify. For objects in the Archive Access or Deep Archive Access tiers of S3 Intelligent\-Tiering, you must first initiate a restore request, and then wait until the object is moved into the Frequent Access tier.
.sp
To restore a specific object version, you can provide a version ID. If you don\(aqt provide a version ID, Amazon S3 restores the current version.
.sp
When restoring an archived object, you can specify one of the following data access tier options in the \fBTier\fP element of the request body:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBExpedited\fP \- Expedited retrievals allow you to quickly access your data stored in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Archive tier when occasional urgent requests for restoring archives are required. For all but the largest archived objects (250 MB+), data accessed using Expedited retrievals is typically made available within 1–5 minutes. Provisioned capacity ensures that retrieval capacity for Expedited retrievals is available when you need it. Expedited retrievals and provisioned capacity are not available for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Deep Archive tier.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStandard\fP \- Standard retrievals allow you to access any of your archived objects within several hours. This is the default option for retrieval requests that do not specify the retrieval option. Standard retrievals typically finish within 3–5 hours for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Archive tier. They typically finish within 12 hours for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Deep Archive tier. Standard retrievals are free for objects stored in S3 Intelligent\-Tiering.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBulk\fP \- Bulk retrievals free for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval and S3 Intelligent\-Tiering storage classes, enabling you to retrieve large amounts, even petabytes, of data at no cost. Bulk retrievals typically finish within 5–12 hours for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Archive tier. Bulk retrievals are also the lowest\-cost retrieval option when restoring objects from S3 Glacier Deep Archive. They typically finish within 48 hours for objects stored in the S3 Glacier Deep Archive storage class or S3 Intelligent\-Tiering Deep Archive tier.
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information about archive retrieval options and provisioned capacity for \fBExpedited\fP data access, see \fI\%Restoring Archived Objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
You can use Amazon S3 restore speed upgrade to change the restore speed to a faster speed while it is in progress. For more information, see \fI\%Upgrading the speed of an in\-progress restore\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
To get the status of object restoration, you can send a \fBHEAD\fP request. Operations return the \fBx\-amz\-restore\fP header, which provides information about the restoration status, in the response. You can use Amazon S3 event notifications to notify you when a restore is initiated or completed. For more information, see \fI\%Configuring Amazon S3 Event Notifications\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
After restoring an archived object, you can update the restoration period by reissuing the request with a new period. Amazon S3 updates the restoration period relative to the current time and charges only for the request\-there are no data transfer charges. You cannot update the restoration period when Amazon S3 is actively processing your current restore request for the object.
.sp
If your bucket has a lifecycle configuration with a rule that includes an expiration action, the object expiration overrides the life span that you specify in a restore request. For example, if you restore an object copy for 10 days, but the object is scheduled to expire in 3 days, Amazon S3 deletes the object in 3 days. For more information about lifecycle configuration, see \fI\%PutBucketLifecycleConfiguration\fP and \fI\%Object Lifecycle Management\fP in \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Responses
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
A successful action returns either the \fB200 OK\fP or \fB202 Accepted\fP status code.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If the object is not previously restored, then Amazon S3 returns \fB202 Accepted\fP in the response.
.IP \(bu 2
If the object is previously restored, Amazon S3 returns \fB200 OK\fP in the response.
.IP \(bu 2
Special errors:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fICode: RestoreAlreadyInProgress\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fICause: Object restore is already in progress.\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fIHTTP Status Code: 409 Conflict\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fISOAP Fault Code Prefix: Client\fP
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fICode: GlacierExpeditedRetrievalNotAvailable\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fICause: expedited retrievals are currently not available. Try again later. (Returned if there is insufficient capacity to process the Expedited request. This error applies only to Expedited retrievals and not to S3 Standard or Bulk retrievals.)\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fIHTTP Status Code: 503\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fISOAP Fault Code Prefix: N/A\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following operations are related to \fBRestoreObject\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%PutBucketLifecycleConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetBucketNotificationConfiguration\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  restore\-object
\-\-bucket <value>
\-\-key <value>
[\-\-version\-id <value>]
[\-\-restore\-request <value>]
[\-\-request\-payer <value>]
[\-\-checksum\-algorithm <value>]
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket name containing the object to restore.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBAccess points\fP \- When you use this action with an access point for general purpose buckets, you must provide the alias of the access point in place of the bucket name or specify the access point ARN. When you use this action with an access point for directory buckets, you must provide the access point name in place of the bucket name. When using the access point ARN, you must direct requests to the access point hostname. The access point hostname takes the form \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .s3\-accesspoint.*Region* .amazonaws.com. When using this action with an access point through the Amazon Web Services SDKs, you provide the access point ARN in place of the bucket name. For more information about access point ARNs, see \fI\%Using access points\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
\fBS3 on Outposts\fP \- When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, you must direct requests to the S3 on Outposts hostname. The S3 on Outposts hostname takes the form \(ga\(ga \fIAccessPointName\fP \-\fIAccountId\fP .*outpostID* .s3\-outposts.*Region* .amazonaws.com\(ga\(ga . When you use this action with S3 on Outposts, the destination bucket must be the Outposts access point ARN or the access point alias. For more information about S3 on Outposts, see \fI\%What is S3 on Outposts?\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-key\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Object key for which the action was initiated.
.sp
Constraints:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
min: \fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-version\-id\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
VersionId used to reference a specific version of the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-restore\-request\fP (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for restore job parameters.
.sp
Days \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Lifetime of the active copy in days. Do not use with restores that specify \fBOutputLocation\fP .
.sp
The Days element is required for regular restores, and must not be provided for select requests.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
GlacierJobParameters \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
S3 Glacier related parameters pertaining to this job. Do not use with restores that specify \fBOutputLocation\fP .
.sp
Tier \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Retrieval tier at which the restore will be processed.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStandard\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBulk\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBExpedited\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Type \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Amazon S3 Select is no longer available to new customers. Existing customers of Amazon S3 Select can continue to use the feature as usual. \fI\%Learn more\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Type of restore request.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSELECT\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Tier \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Retrieval tier at which the restore will be processed.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBStandard\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBulk\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBExpedited\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Description \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The optional description for the job.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
SelectParameters \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Amazon S3 Select is no longer available to new customers. Existing customers of Amazon S3 Select can continue to use the feature as usual. \fI\%Learn more\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Describes the parameters for Select job types.
.sp
InputSerialization \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes the serialization format of the object.
.sp
CSV \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes the serialization of a CSV\-encoded object.
.sp
FileHeaderInfo \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes the first line of input. Valid values are:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNONE\fP : First line is not a header.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIGNORE\fP : First line is a header, but you can\(aqt use the header values to indicate the column in an expression. You can use column position (such as _1, _2, …) to indicate the column (\fBSELECT s._1 FROM OBJECT s\fP ).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUse\fP : First line is a header, and you can use the header value to identify a column in an expression (\fBSELECT \(dqname\(dq FROM OBJECT\fP ).
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUSE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIGNORE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNONE\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Comments \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used to indicate that a row should be ignored when the character is present at the start of that row. You can specify any character to indicate a comment line. The default character is \fB#\fP .
.sp
Default: \fB#\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
QuoteEscapeCharacter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used for escaping the quotation mark character inside an already escaped value. For example, the value \fB\(dq\(dq\(dq a , b \(dq\(dq\(dq\fP is parsed as \fB\(dq a , b \(dq\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RecordDelimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used to separate individual records in the input. Instead of the default value, you can specify an arbitrary delimiter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
FieldDelimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used to separate individual fields in a record. You can specify an arbitrary delimiter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
QuoteCharacter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used for escaping when the field delimiter is part of the value. For example, if the value is \fBa, b\fP , Amazon S3 wraps this field value in quotation marks, as follows: \fB\(dq a , b \(dq\fP .
.sp
Type: String
.sp
Default: \fB\(dq\fP
.sp
Ancestors: \fBCSV\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
AllowQuotedRecordDelimiter \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies that CSV field values may contain quoted record delimiters and such records should be allowed. Default value is FALSE. Setting this value to TRUE may lower performance.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CompressionType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies object\(aqs compression format. Valid values: NONE, GZIP, BZIP2. Default Value: NONE.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNONE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGZIP\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBZIP2\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
JSON \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies JSON as object\(aqs input serialization format.
.sp
Type \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The type of JSON. Valid values: Document, Lines.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDOCUMENT\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLINES\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Parquet \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies Parquet as object\(aqs input serialization format.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ExpressionType \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The type of the provided expression (for example, SQL).
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSQL\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Expression \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Amazon S3 Select is no longer available to new customers. Existing customers of Amazon S3 Select can continue to use the feature as usual. \fI\%Learn more\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The expression that is used to query the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
OutputSerialization \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes how the results of the Select job are serialized.
.sp
CSV \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes the serialization of CSV\-encoded Select results.
.sp
QuoteFields \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether to use quotation marks around output fields.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBALWAYS\fP : Always use quotation marks for output fields.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBASNEEDED\fP : Use quotation marks for output fields when needed.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBALWAYS\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBASNEEDED\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
QuoteEscapeCharacter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The single character used for escaping the quote character inside an already escaped value.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RecordDelimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used to separate individual records in the output. Instead of the default value, you can specify an arbitrary delimiter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
FieldDelimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The value used to separate individual fields in a record. You can specify an arbitrary delimiter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
QuoteCharacter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A single character used for escaping when the field delimiter is part of the value. For example, if the value is \fBa, b\fP , Amazon S3 wraps this field value in quotation marks, as follows: \fB\(dq a , b \(dq\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
JSON \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies JSON as request\(aqs output serialization format.
.sp
RecordDelimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The value used to separate individual records in the output. If no value is specified, Amazon S3 uses a newline character (\(aqn\(aq).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
OutputLocation \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes the location where the restore job\(aqs output is stored.
.sp
S3 \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Describes an S3 location that will receive the results of the restore request.
.sp
BucketName \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the bucket where the restore results will be placed.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Prefix \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The prefix that is prepended to the restore results for this request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Encryption \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Contains the type of server\-side encryption used.
.sp
EncryptionType \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The server\-side encryption algorithm used when storing job results in Amazon S3 (for example, AES256, \fBaws:kms\fP ).
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAES256\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:fsx\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:kms\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws:kms:dsse\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
KMSKeyId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If the encryption type is \fBaws:kms\fP , this optional value specifies the ID of the symmetric encryption customer managed key to use for encryption of job results. Amazon S3 only supports symmetric encryption KMS keys. For more information, see \fI\%Asymmetric keys in KMS\fP in the \fIAmazon Web Services Key Management Service Developer Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
KMSContext \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If the encryption type is \fBaws:kms\fP , this optional value can be used to specify the encryption context for the restore results.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CannedACL \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The canned ACL to apply to the restore results.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBprivate\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpublic\-read\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpublic\-read\-write\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauthenticated\-read\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBaws\-exec\-read\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbucket\-owner\-read\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbucket\-owner\-full\-control\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
AccessControlList \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A list of grants that control access to the staged results.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for grant information.
.sp
Grantee \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The person being granted permissions.
.sp
DisplayName \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Screen name of the grantee.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
EmailAddress \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Email address of the grantee.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Using email addresses to specify a grantee is only supported in the following Amazon Web Services Regions:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
US East (N. Virginia)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (N. California)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (Oregon)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Singapore)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Sydney)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Tokyo)
.IP \(bu 2
Europe (Ireland)
.IP \(bu 2
South America (São Paulo)
.UNINDENT
.sp
For a list of all the Amazon S3 supported Regions and endpoints, see \fI\%Regions and Endpoints\fP in the Amazon Web Services General Reference.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ID \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The canonical user ID of the grantee.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Type \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Type of grantee
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCanonicalUser\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAmazonCustomerByEmail\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGroup\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
URI \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
URI of the grantee group.
.UNINDENT
